9.4 Critical MCP stdout requirement

For an MCP server using standard input/output transport, stdout is reserved for JSON-RPC protocol messages.

Do not globally redirect stdout with:

python
sys.stdout = sys.stderr


Application logs or console output written to stdout can corrupt MCP messages.

If you see:

text
Failed to parse JSONRPC message from server


inspect the captured input for unexpected console output, progress bars, ANSI color sequences, logging messages, or encoding errors.

A local redirect_stdout block may help with ordinary Python output during graph execution, but it is not a universal solution for logging handlers that retain their own output stream.

Configure the relevant loggers and handlers explicitly if the error persists.

Also verify the indentation of the with block around the tutor_graph.ainvoke(state) call.

9.5 MCP versus REST

The REST API and MCP server are separate entry points:

REST API: main.py, started with Uvicorn.
MCP server: mcp_server.py, normally started by an MCP-compatible client using stdio transport.

The MCP server is not automatically available as an HTTP endpoint just because the FastAPI service is deployed.

A separate MCP deployment or transport configuration may be needed if remote MCP access is required.

